  "conclusions": [
    "ACT DR6 plus BOSS supplies finite, correlated, angular/window-weighted E_G estimates for CMASS and LOWZ at effective redshifts 0.555 and 0.316; it does not directly supply a continuous local E_G(N,k).",
    "The paper reports scale-binned E_G and two combined amplitudes, with additional correlated ACT+Planck combinations; these are not four independent redshift measurements.",
    "The imported beta is a galaxy-sample RSD fit using fiducial power shape/amplitude, nonlinear-bias and effective-theory modeling and free Alcock-Paczynski parameters; it is not continuous R or P3.",
    "1210.0439v2 is an ideal-observability analysis under explicit matter, bias, frame and linear assumptions, with further quasistatic/sound-horizon assumptions for its Horndeski shape tests; it contains no released P3 measurements.",
    "Sigma_A=Y(1+eta), L_A and P2_A=L_A/R in 1210.0439v2 have twice the normalization of the standard lensing Sigma, L and ACT E_G. P2_A=2 E_G; P3 is invariant under the constant rescaling.",
    "Source velocity symbols have different printed signs. Use an explicit metric/Fourier/velocity dictionary anchored to E_G^GR=Omega_m0/f before importing formulas.",
    "Neither the two amplitudes nor the binned projected statistics supply the required time derivatives, continuous same-mode scale derivatives, or a physical F history without an additional model, boundary data, calibrations and a likelihood/window reconstruction.",
    "Public underlying catalogue/map products and named analysis packages were located. Article-specific numerical E_G/cross-spectrum bandpower arrays, exact window matrices, joint covariance and beta likelihood release were not independently verified in this bounded documentation search; the paper promises availability upon publication. This is not a claim that such products do not exist.",
    "All published summaries read here are exposed development information, not holdouts. The result is a bounded input-admission limitation, not a universal no-go for lensing/growth or an exclusion/confirmation of the root candidate."
  ],
